Debian packaging prototype for swsml (libswsml)
==============================================

STATUS: PROTOTYPE — NOT BUILT OR VERIFIED ON THE AUTHOR'S MACHINE.

The working, validated packaging path is `packaging/build_deb.sh`
(dpkg-deb --build, no debhelper). That script produced and smoke-tested
four .deb files on WSL/Ubuntu. This debian/ tree is a starting point for a
future formal debhelper (dh) build; it has not been exercised here.

Package split (by backend, headers not mixed):
  libswsml0        runtime  : libswsml.so.0 (Rust cdylib C-ABI)
  libswsml-dev     C dev    : sml_rs.h + libswsml.so + swsml.pc
  libswsml-cpp0    C++ rt   : libswsml_cpp.so.0 (RAII wrapper)
  libswsml-cpp-dev C++ dev  : sml_rs.hpp + libswsml_cpp.so + swsml_cpp.pc

Conventions:
  * Names avoid the Debian libSML / libsml-dev (smart-meter) collision.
  * Runtime package trailing digit == SONAME major (SONAME_MAJOR=0).
  * pkg-config modules are `swsml` / `swsml_cpp` (not `sml`).
  * libswsml-dev installs ONLY sml_rs.h (never sml.h / sml_codes.h).

To try (on a Debian/Ubuntu host with the Build-Depends installed):
  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
